 bodies  or murderer if you want to call it where  you don't know anymore what is true what  is who's lying where am i and this house  becomes a character by itself that you  know  you don't even know anymore where which  room is the map of the house becomes  very blurry as if you took some lsd and  so i always you told each other all the  time like it should be like a drug  infused trip if you know the moment that  there's a moment in the film that beast  eats the cake and they tell her you know  i hope you realize this weed cake but  you already ate like literally half the  cake right and it doesn't really make  her stone but it does make her go into  this rabbit hole like alice in  wonderland and you know and the rest is  sort of a mental trip oh totally i  definitely felt that and like you  mentioned too i like that immersive feel  like i felt like i was at the party with  them  um  also was there any choices for you as a  director when you look back that you  were like the most hung up on like was  there anything that was making you like  toss and turn at night  um oh yeah i mean you mean for me myself  like what i was nervous about yeah like  was there something you kind of just  didn't know which way to go with like  what was that thing that you were like  oh  i mean the ending i mean can we i don't  know how much we can spoil it yeah this  is spoiler yeah okay spoiler so um here  we go with spoilers so for me when i got  on board of this project i was very  intrigued by the game because i used to  play that game all the time with my  friends and it was like psychological  warfare and i thought it was a great  premise for you know a juicy character  piece  uh but the end at that time there was  still a killer uh and i was not  interested in that because for me not  because i judge it at all because i love  great films with great killers or  monsters or a haunted house or a ghost  or whatever but it's just not my style i  come from a very different background 