eling for me personally is  like what you know because it's so  it is like on purpose of course  nihilistic lame you could even call it  like it's just like a big balloon and  all the air flows out and i love that so  i think but i hope in the end that you  had a good time that you had some laughs  and that you maybe have a little bit of  thought about you know what we are  capable  as far as group behavior you know how we  sometimes just i think the truth this is  of course a more a dark comedy than a  horror but the horror of the thing to me  is human behavior you know where  misunderstandings can lead to something  like this and also just  i often compare them to a school of fish  you know there's one  yeah the whole group goes that way and  they're not actually looking at what's  going on because they're constantly  glued to their phone screen and when the  wi-fi goes out the demons come in so  i hope that it maybe will provoke some  discussion but mainly of course i hope  to entertain people and just make them  laugh and make them feel something and a  little bit afraid but also just this  haunting feeling of this weird trip and  this weird house you know so i hope they  enjoyed themselves yeah hell yeah and  you know everyone listen to this  interview go see it again tell your  friends about it make sure to see it in  theaters first then get hyped for the  blu-ray it sounds like it's gonna be a  lot of cool stuff with it helena thank  you so much for joining me today and i  hope to talk to you again in the future  thank you so much i love this  conversation it was really amazing thank  you so much for having me you're very  very kind thank you oh thank you  appreciate you

